From bbe76fef31015a71fb9bd228b59b7f3b243aec0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ktiays <cuansky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:53:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Build libdispatch for Emscripten wasm32

Add an Emscripten event backend (a manager thread waiting on a monotonic
condition variable for pokes and timers; descriptor and signal sources do
not register), a run-loop handle that is a receive right of the in-process
Mach library the port supplies, futex wait and wake over Emscripten's
primitives with an unfair lock that waits on its word, and the Emscripten
branches for headers, clocks, byte order, CPU counts, thread ids and the
program name. Fix the release's non-Darwin build: the scrubbed OS version
check and the main-thread thread-event constants only Darwin defines.
